      "stem": "Find the $n$th term of $10, 7, 4, 1, ...$.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$-3n + 13$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$-3n + 10$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$3n + 7$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$10 - n$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "The common difference is $-3$, so the $n$th term starts with $-3n$. When $n = 1$: $-3(1) = -3$, but the first term is $10$, so we add $13$. The $n$th term is $-3n + 13$."
    }
